WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.173
Collagen cream does not
replace your collagen.

00:00:02.173 --> 00:00:05.212
Collagen powder does not travel
straight to your face.

00:00:05.562 --> 00:00:06.562
So where does it go?

00:00:06.582 --> 00:00:08.197
23 trials say the powder works.

00:00:08.413 --> 00:00:11.701
Remove the industry funded ones,
and watch what happens.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.593
But first, what protects the
collagen you already have?

00:00:14.943 --> 00:00:16.169
Think of your skin
as a building.

00:00:16.169 --> 00:00:18.540
Collagen is the main
structure inside it.

00:00:18.775 --> 00:00:20.544
It keeps everything firm and upright.

00:00:20.844 --> 00:00:23.175
As we age, collagen production slows.

00:00:23.391 --> 00:00:27.322
And ultraviolet light switches on
enzymes that cut collagen apart.

00:00:27.538 --> 00:00:29.928
The sun runs a demolition
crew. It works weekends.

00:00:30.228 --> 00:00:31.617
Sunscreen is not just about sunburn.

00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:34.786
It draws a boundary
around the building.

00:00:35.207 --> 00:00:38.630
Preserving collagen is usually easier
than replacing it later.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:39.980
Now, the cream.

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:43.341
To pass through skin, a molecule
generally needs to be under

00:00:43.341 --> 00:00:44.701
about 500 daltons.

00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:46.645
Collagen is around 300,000.

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:48.701
It is not getting
through that door.

00:00:49.001 --> 00:00:52.418
It may still form a
moisturising film on the surface.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.112
Skin may feel smoother.

00:00:54.394 --> 00:00:56.854
But polishing the windows is
not replacing the beams.

00:00:57.204 --> 00:00:58.338
Now, the powder.

00:00:58.338 --> 00:01:02.548
Swallow collagen, and digestion breaks it
into peptides and amino acids.

00:01:02.764 --> 00:01:04.978
Your stomach does not
offer facial delivery.

00:01:05.278 --> 00:01:06.743
Some pieces may be absorbed.

00:01:06.959 --> 00:01:08.730
Certain peptides may even
act as signals.

00:01:08.897 --> 00:01:11.041
But your body decides
where they go.

00:01:11.041 --> 00:01:14.089
Skin, joints, tendons, wherever
repairs are most urgent.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:15.589
Your face ordered scaffolding.

00:01:15.663 --> 00:01:18.017
It got a box
of spare parts.

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.036
Does the powder work?

00:01:20.036 --> 00:01:24.258
Trials do report modest
improvements in hydration,

00:01:24.258 --> 00:01:26.036
elasticity, or wrinkles.

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:29.618
But many were small,
short, and industry funded.

00:01:29.918 --> 00:01:33.653
In 2025, researchers pooled
23 randomised trials.

00:01:34.086 --> 00:01:35.114
All together, a benefit.

00:01:35.114 --> 00:01:37.575
Keep only the studies
without industry funding,

00:01:37.575 --> 00:01:39.913
and it is no
longer statistically significant.

00:01:40.129 --> 00:01:42.981
Keep only the higher
quality studies. Same result.

00:01:43.197 --> 00:01:44.494
The effect stops showing up.

00:01:44.794 --> 00:01:46.239
Do supplements definitely work?

00:01:46.515 --> 00:01:48.639
We cannot say that. Definitely fail?

00:01:48.855 --> 00:01:50.565
We cannot confidently say that either.

00:01:50.781 --> 00:01:52.476
The independent evidence is uncertain.

00:01:53.026 --> 00:01:54.526
What the evidence actually supports.

00:01:54.526 --> 00:01:59.984
Broad spectrum sunscreen, every
day. Not smoking.

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:01.724
Enough protein and vitamin C.

00:02:01.724 --> 00:02:05.994
And for suitable users, topical retinoids
have considerably stronger evidence for

00:02:05.994 --> 00:02:08.605
encouraging collagen production than collagen cream.

00:02:08.905 --> 00:02:10.942
Collagen cream can be
a pleasant moisturiser.

00:02:10.942 --> 00:02:12.570
Collagen powder is optional.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.634
Protect the building before you
buy expensive powdered bricks.
